				<td align="left" class="TextMain">
					<center><h2> Guild Rules And Conduct</h2></center>
					We are who were once a rag tag collection of motley individuals have come 
					together and become a whole, greater than the sum of its parts. We stand 
					together against all adversaries and obstacles. Our alligence to our own is 
					first and foremost. we are family. It is the belief and practice of our guild to 
					help those in need. we do not shirk in these duties. Loyalty and honor are codes 
					by which we live and revier. If whomever you may be should be so fortunate as to 
					be counted as one of our number, rejoice for you have gained a new family, new 
					friends. Woe betide those who would make an enemy of you for he has made an 
					enemy of us all, for we are legion. <BR><BR>
					
					<h3>Guild Documents</h3>
					<blockquote>
					<strong><a href=rules.asp>Rules and Conduct For Members</a></strong> - The following rules of conduct 
					and guidelines have been set forth as to make our playing time more 
					enjoyable and fruitful, and not as a means to take away from 
					the total gaming experience. All members agree to abide by them.<BR><BR>
					<strong><a href=oconduct.asp>Rules and Conduct For Officers</a></strong> - The following rules of conduct 
					and guidelines have been set forth for officers.  All officers agree to
					do their very best to live by them.  
					<BR><BR>
					</blockquote>
				</td>
